course: dictionary
lesson: 14105
title: Merging: joining together
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Merging is the -ing form of the verb «merge». To merge means to join together into one. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it for clues. «The two lanes are merging into one at the bridge.» The lanes are joining together, so merging means joining together into one.
explain: Merging can also be a noun, meaning the act of joining. «The merging of the two schools made one big school.» Here merging names the whole event of joining. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "The joining together of the two schools made one big school" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Road signs use merging to warn drivers. A «Merging traffic» sign means cars from another road are about to join your lane. Words like traffic and lanes are the clues that tell you the meaning.
fact: Merging is the -ing form of the verb «merge».
fact: «Merge» means to join together into one.
fact: As a noun, «merging» means the act of joining.
fact: A «Merging traffic» sign warns drivers that cars from another road are joining their lane.
fact: Context clues, such as traffic or lanes, can help you work out what merging means.
exercise: «The two lanes are merging into one at the bridge.» What does merging mean here? | Splitting apart into many | Stopping suddenly | *Joining together into one | Going backwards
exercise: «The rivers are merging near the old mill.» What is happening to the rivers? | *Joining together into one | Freezing solid | Drying up completely | Running uphill
exercise: Ella sees a sign that says «Merging traffic». What should she expect? | Cars stopping for a picnic | Cars driving in reverse | A long line of boats | *Cars from another road joining her lane
test: «The merging of the two teams made one strong squad.» In this sentence, what is merging? | A type of fast car | A loud noise | *The act of joining together | A team that has lost
test: Which word means joining together into one? | folder | file | computer | *merging
exam: «The two streams are merging into one wide river.» What does merging mean? | Turning to ice | Growing very tall | Running away from each other | *Joining together into one
